answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285099}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "60ebcac8-bc59-5dde-9394-be5d3c916d93" :question/math-academy-id "q-142112" :question/problem "Which of the following shaded areas describes the region bounded by the inequality $x+2y\\le 4?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the inequality into slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2y & \\le 4 \\\\ 2y & \\le -x+4 \\\\ y & \\le -\\frac{1}{2}x+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we proceed as usual. We start by drawing the corresponding straight line \n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{2}x+2.\n$$\n\n Since the inequality involves a 'less than *or equal to*' sign, the line $y=-\\frac{1}{2}x+2$ itself is part of the solution. Therefore, we draw a **solid line**. \n\nThen, we need to decide whether to shade above or below the line. The inequality \n\n$$\ny\\le -\\frac{1}{2}x+2\n$$\n\n refers to the $y$-values that are *less than* or equal to those on the line $y=-\\frac{1}{2}x+2,$ so we shade *below* the line. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/8b906cf167528f484109528a93732dc2b8d73558bb02f454bb520af87efde3c5.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285105 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "031f0fd6-385d-56b8-9e8e-b264e6e89ed3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Graph of a Non-Strict Inequality Given in Standard Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da2d4eba-9681-5c20-aa56-5bc930b166e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/5456e2ee349d219f3072d305415c939d5d4a3b0cbc189b55be3102fb5c72a3a7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285107} {:answer/id #uuid "b6684340-75bf-50f2-8dbd-b881f1f05820" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/8e7f4a75c7793e4770643cc40decbfd007f7809f96475a914c5c00d4f5ee13bc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285108} {:answer/id #uuid "8d9c1cac-5995-595a-8ef2-04e50db59b74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/35e2d168ece734f2bc84a3b9c41208cb941fabbf8b4c9b1de600f8c5dad5ac1d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285109} {:answer/id #uuid "4aa3ca47-844b-5023-9f52-4e8e676b34e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/2a46c79189ad438d1c4bd1528e50e93881bbf7690d37b16b9ebeaaa44bff06a8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285110} {:answer/id #uuid "54e5ec57-bac5-5cca-971c-8ae35bf37d08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/5f7df5dc434ecc1a04fc60aa476303db2ccea9dda6b8a9fa28eae5dedddc44b6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285111}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6684340-75bf-50f2-8dbd-b881f1f05820" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/8e7f4a75c7793e4770643cc40decbfd007f7809f96475a914c5c00d4f5ee13bc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285108} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3af5ebc-bf75-5ada-b49a-3e620b7e319e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285106}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6025b073-9e75-57a3-a820-ad415f72c95d" :question/math-academy-id "q-142113" :question/problem "Which of the following shaded areas describes the region bounded by the inequality $2x+4y\\ge 8?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the inequality into slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+4y & \\ge 8 \\\\ 4y & \\ge -2x+8 \\\\ y & \\ge -\\frac{1}{2}x+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we proceed as usual. We start by drawing the corresponding straight line \n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{2}x+2.\n$$\n\n Since the inequality involves a 'greater than *or equal to*' sign, the line $y=-\\frac{1}{2}x+2$ itself is part of the solution. Therefore, we draw a **solid line**.\n\nThen, we need to decide whether to shade above or below the line. The inequality \n\n$$\ny\\ge -\\frac{1}{2}x+2\n$$\n\n refers to the $y$-values that are *greater than* or equal to those on the line $y=-\\frac{1}{2}x+2,$ so we shade *above* the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/226415c7de8240eaa2a87a10e87d95c6dbf45df6263c4b36ea819cfec097a8a0.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285112 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "031f0fd6-385d-56b8-9e8e-b264e6e89ed3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Graph of a Non-Strict Inequality Given in Standard Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31101cb1-3114-5f57-bb11-2f764bec9899" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/ae74be6af41cbfd239e15f7bb2e2e09504dbb718c3f308ab41157a6251daad01.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285114} {:answer/id #uuid "efb0296d-7483-52b0-881b-caddfb80a6ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/6bc89797cabfa5cc5e1baec5bf576fd81e4dd48fb9ff646009bd6cdad7e42c73.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285115} {:answer/id #uuid "0b1a224e-2cb8-53a0-827a-ec15f0c1d25d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/418e4724130ac11b03ea2b293f36e81d712a5364ed5addf70ae2900ef196d650.png" :d