the line. The inequality \n\n$$\ny\\le \\frac{3}{2}x-3\n$$\n\n refers to the $y$-values that are *less than* or equal to those on the line $y=\\frac{3}{2}x-3,$ so we shade *below* the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/ea12ed8d62304ecdc90859d5cd206045cef852522ce16c67a9307ddbd755b3dc.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285119 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ecbf45e4-67a6-58cd-9655-4a339de64db5" :knowledge-point/title "Inequalities Involving Horizontal and Vertical Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46f65787-a4ad-5199-888b-306abcd589fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285121} {:answer/id #uuid "1462eb16-c711-59e6-b4e7-3b7f37aed81e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285122}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1462eb16-c711-59e6-b4e7-3b7f37aed81e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285122} :answer-field/id #uuid "5550bb69-1f66-51f6-a769-255032a6ab59" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285120} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8e73c95-4aef-5553-ad18-a6a88451efd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285124} {:answer/id #uuid "f521c672-f8b9-518d-9bfd-4f3a7041e2dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285125} {:answer/id #uuid "9e0cfcd6-014f-59e6-933c-0da358c23b45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285126} {:answer/id #uuid "1a087095-9176-57c8-a34a-8b633e67df30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285127}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e0cfcd6-014f-59e6-933c-0da358c23b45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285126} :answer-field/id #uuid "86b39e87-8c8e-5412-9e81-d90257281abf" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285123}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fae4dc0d-5fcc-556e-856f-aa7c560289fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-214907" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/cb311261eabb4b5c1b6c4114c92e798f0caf2e326dc90486429d230167f6978b.png)\n\nExpress the shaded region above as an inequality.The shaded region above is described by the inequality\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The border-line is a vertical line passing through the point $(-2,0).$ Therefore, the line has the equation $x=-2.$\n\nNow, we need to decide which inequality symbol to use. Since the line is dashed, we will use a strict inequality. Since the shaded region is to the *right* of the line, the inequality refers to the $x$-values that are *greater than* those on the line $x=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\nx>-2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285128 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ecbf45e4-67a6-58cd-9655-4a339de64db5" :knowledge-point/title "Inequalities Involving Horizontal and Vertical Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fb71d81-bcee-5ace-a028-62e2e6f1ddce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285130} {:answer/id #uuid "95dcee54-b96f-5308-81f7-afb17d874eb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285131}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95dcee54-b96f-5308-81f7-afb17d874eb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285131} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf57dc5e