x$-values that are *less than or equal to* those on the line $x=-1.$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\nx\\le -1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184679 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ecbf45e4-67a6-58cd-9655-4a339de64db5" :knowledge-point/title "Inequalities Involving Horizontal and Vertical Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e7e6be5-fcec-5ddd-b8fd-3a9858fdd4e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y > - 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186182969} {:answer/id #uuid "bff8dfbd-a150-5171-8d51-684ea0bff1fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\ge - 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186182970} {:answer/id #uuid "2f535254-3173-5d4a-8af9-ceebc5372716" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y \\le - 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186182971} {:answer/id #uuid "347bc70b-a147-5285-945c-8f101a52342c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y < x - 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186182972} {:answer/id #uuid "3f7479d8-7dee-551a-839a-ae78644b1bd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x > - 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186182973}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f7479d8-7dee-551a-839a-ae78644b1bd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x > - 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186182973} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e4ff889-23e6-508c-b9c3-5b46b80e0a00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186182968}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ece6fc50-0ed1-527d-8b93-8f3b5d41e6ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-29423" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/dcfffb2c9005da34a529cdf5ef372bdac840a1308b92507ad0ea0a5359a1387f.png)\n\nFind the inequality that describes the shaded region shown above." :question/worked-solution "The border-line is a vertical line passing through the point $(-4,0).$ Therefore, the line has the equation $x=-4.$\n\nNow, we need to decide which inequality symbol to use. Since the line is dashed, we will use a strict inequality. Since the shaded region is to the *right* of the line, the inequality refers to the $x$-values that are *greater than* those on the line $x=-4.$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\nx>-4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285137 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ecbf45e4-67a6-58cd-9655-4a339de64db5" :knowledge-point/title "Inequalities Involving Horizontal and Vertical Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af7af458-acee-5de8-9a35-a2daeafc2fa0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x>2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285139} {:answer/id #uuid "0c57c29f-e8df-5b13-ae84-409da2fb7177" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\le 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285140} {:answer/id #uuid "19c83f6f-5be1-58b6-b4f8-fa2a93e8008a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y>x+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285141} {:answer/id #uuid "518cae7a-9824-53c4-a09f-077f9223ee9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285142} {:answer/id #uuid "01ad819b-aa4f-595b-bc07-9ea5de110c5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\ge 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285143}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01ad819b-aa4f-595b-bc07-9ea5de110c5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\ge 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285143} :answer-field/id #uuid "080641ca-4845-5e66-b1f3-ef1302b7f255" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285138}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4ef15986-247a-5c73-9a2b-17e3295a31c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-44558" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/daa0365127a12a9a561d0790af855b5f26f8ab9188ac541b142cd9d9e0a919cc.png)\n\nFind the inequality that describes the shaded region shown above." :question/worked-solution "The border-line is a horizontal line passing through the point $(0,2).$ Therefore, the line has the equation $y=2.$\n\nNow, we need to decide which inequality symbol to use. Since the line is solid, we will use an \"or equal to\" inequality. Since the shaded region is *above* the line, the inequality refers to the $y$-values that are *greater than or equal to* those on the line $y=2.$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\ge 2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285144 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9ceefc-3aa8-5c13-90a1-e4a084f720cc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Graph of a Strict Inequality Given in Standard Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a525b07-e3cc-5e72-89eb-50c7ab915546" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/e68e5e19e2ed63a4f9c1b65f8af7bed53568d304c3b0ce916617f1f305db3b2c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285146} {:answer/id #uuid "14448a5b-bb66-54aa-99b1-eb946b5af64a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/06a904255ae51542be4dd3bab0edf54bf9d3cc3cd32a2ae07f442e5114db46ce.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285147} {:answer/id #uuid "5922e4dc-ec15-5b3e-80b9-a74c54c3ff13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/c7892faf71691acb91e82a78f43df86797bade59037d25746f88f93a7fde55f2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285148} {:answer/id #uuid "5204d138-bfe1-5786-9f86-cadd0f66b85e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/07de9cd8bb359093767ba2dfe9e762ca602d97dbe7b1217541fe4b5017675162.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285149} {:answer/id #uuid "85cd257a-a9cb-5577-927e-d69c137c33d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/6f80afd5890da875ba16684156e673f3a368904b11c056a72841cf6237ccab21.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285150}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5204d138-bfe1-5786-9f86-cadd0f66b85e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/07de9cd8bb359093767ba2dfe9e762ca602d97dbe7b1217541fe4b5017675162.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285149} :answer-field/id #uuid "6eeb5efd-2ee9-55d3-8ba3-33ff2e6119a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285145}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8a7533fa-9ecc-5c43-b4ae-5837f068bca8" :question/math-academy-id "q-64020" :question/problem "Which of the following shaded areas describes the region bounded by the inequality $8x-4y<12?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the inequality into slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8x-4y & <12 \\\\ -4y & <-8x+12 \\\\ 4y & >8x-12 \\\\ y & >2x-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we proceed as usual. We start by drawing the corresponding straight line $y=2x-3.$ Since the inequality involves a 'strictly greater than' sign, the line $y=2x-3$ itself is *not* part of the solution. Therefore, we draw a dashed line.\n\nThen, we need to decide whether to shade above or below the line. The inequality $y>2x-3$ refers to the $y$-values that are *greater than* those on the line $y=2x-3,$ so we shade *above* the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/d399f186d02b777d8b6774833cd9e0855de5f228b1e6872027d7909d2e6dbe6f.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184763 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9ceefc-3aa8-5c13-90a1-e4a084f720cc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Graph of a Strict Inequality Given in Standard Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4e32104-d791-5438-ab97-4cc9b0bfa82f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3822/Source/Images/q-64021-a-3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183468} {:answer/id #uuid "d541815a-4985-59b1-929a-ffbfe0ee47af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3822/Source/Images/q-64021-a-4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183469} {:answer/id #uuid "eba996f7-152f-5f25-986d-6dc1fa776e1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3822/Source/Images/q-64021-a-2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183470} {:answer/id #uuid "f00eb402-959a-520f-b060-d07b4a0cbaad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3822/Source/Images/q-64021-a-5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183471} {:answer/id #uuid "73a85cff-10b5-5b64-90e6-d9bc6bdb16b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3822/Source/Images/q-64021-a-1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183472}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73a85cff-10b5-5b64-90e6-d9bc6bdb16b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3822/Source/Images/q-64021-a-1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183472} :answer-field/id #uuid "2db80fdb-51a9-5ff9-94c9-13a46bda4fff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183467}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f54dc8b4-bdaf-5005-8cdd-60add97ff7c2" :question/math-academy-id "q-64021" :question/problem "Which of the following shaded areas describes the region bounded by the inequality $x-y<3?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the inequality into slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-y & <3 \\\\ -y & <-x+3 \\\\ y & >x-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we proceed as usual. We start by drawing the corresponding straight line \n\n$$\ny=x-3.\n$$\n\n Since the inequality involves a 'strictly greater than' sign, the line $y=x-3$ itself is *not* part of the solution. Therefore, we draw a **dashed line**.\n\nThen, we need to decide whether to shade above or below the line. The inequality \n\n$$\ny>x-3\n$$\n\n refers to the $y$-values that are *greater than* those on the line $y=x-3,$ so we shade *above* the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/77a4c9b6bc705a2fbf486bfef5a6ce57924aae86c4abf1510040c7957b873329.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285151 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9ceefc-3aa8-5c13-90a1-e4a084f720cc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Graph of a Strict Inequality Given in Standard Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc19e693-d8bf-5ae7-b4c8-9c5d1034c3fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/9c03e15abc255bcc4fecf6ba6f617639ee06e2720c81891a936ba906ae6c83f2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285153} {:answer/id #uuid "c2c7c168-866b-50a6-8068-09b87d0d5f0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/baba27c5989981679ac5e5290db3b88803f892659869b54991b17a0b1574e422.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285154} {:answer/id #uuid "7913228d-237a-5aa3-b357-25262c48890b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/a50effb3acd9884ab7f351a820720a0a3ab7728c9242c576a17ddc58ad2d7111.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285155} {:answer/id #uuid "5abc9aec-21b6-512a-8422-7942f4273eea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/c60ad7f7e7e4f801102359920f17320370657445ab6d3cd58865184dd8bcdb28.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285156} {:answer/id #uuid "3b8b15be-b418-5cb6-be97-7a3926d4c2a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/0541476ba87e303dd3209dd6ec5cb848dcf965fc82d42ca93c91f0865bb7de9c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285157}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2c7c168-866b-50a6-8068-09b87d0d5f0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/baba27c5989981679ac5e5290db3b88803f892659869b54991b17a0b1574e422.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285154} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad757d07-1b4b-5166-8293-95a6383b15d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285152}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6a1e5f6d-8386-5d50-83c0-4d415e2103b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-64023" :question/problem "Which of the following shaded areas describes the region bounded by the inequality $x-y>-5?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the inequality into slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-y & >-5 \\\\ -y & >-x-5 \\\\ y & <x+5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we proceed as usual. We start by drawing the corresponding straight line $y=x+5.$ Since the inequality involves a 'strictly less than' sign, the line $y=x+5$ itself is *not* part of the solution. Therefore, we draw a dashed line.\n\nThen, we need to decide whether to shade above or below the line. The inequality $y<x+5$ refers to the $y$-values that are *less than* those on the line $y=x+5,$ so we shade *below* the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/bd0ce52fe5aaf5e95c4f2eb5bd14652ee696c7bb2dfdb99ccdf07543be46f45e.png)"}]}
